{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFollow-up to the `scanner-integration` incident and ticket `90c7-c465-4037-42d5`.\nThe original plan included guarding `.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml`, but that workflow\nand `scripts/install_review_scanners.py` are absent from current `origin/main` after revert\n`9c7d78127696`. This ticket therefore does **not** recreate or re-land the scanner lane. The\nscanner lane re-land is owned by a separate later ticket.\n\nTwo general-purpose hardening gaps still exist on main:\n\n1. `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` keeps a hardcoded workflow tuple. That lets a\n   newly wired reusable workflow escape the predates-gate guard invariant until someone remembers to\n   add it to the tuple.\n2. `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` currently performs no static bash-only-construct scan of\n   CI-reachable make recipes. The module runs workflow step bodies under bash, but GNU make executes\n   recipe lines under `/bin/sh` unless a recipe explicitly selects another shell. On Ubuntu that is\n   dash, and dash does not reject `set -o pipefail` at parse time. A static text scan is therefore\n   needed to catch bash-only tokens before a lane can vote green without executing the intended\n   recipe.\n\nADR 0114 applies to new required CI gates. This ticket only strengthens unit tests exercised by the\nexisting suite; it does not add or promote a CI voting lane.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. In `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`, derive `GUARDED_WORKFLOWS` from the local\n   `uses:` transitive closure rooted at `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` and\n   `.github/workflows/test.yml`. Keep the former hardcoded workflow list as a required floor and\n   assert the derived set is a superset, so any reusable workflow wired into the gating/mirror lanes\n   enters the predates-gate guard invariant immediately, including a future scanner lane re-land.\n2. In `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, derive the CI-reachable make recipe set from the\n   workflow commands that invoke `make` in the gating/mirror lanes, then follow `$(MAKE) <target>`\n   edges transitively. On current main this includes the direct CI entry targets `lint`, `typecheck`,\n   `config-check`, and `e2e-deps`, and the `lint` child target `actionlint-bin`; it excludes dev-only\n   targets that CI does not invoke. Add a static text scan over that derived target set and fail on\n   non-POSIX-dash constructs: `set -o pipefail`, `[[ ... ]]`, indexed or associative arrays,\n   here-strings `<<<`, and `${var^}` / `${var,}` case-modification. Prefer a direct pattern scan over\n   hand-rolling a shell parser; ShellCheck is already available as an executable through the repo's\n   tooling, but this invariant needs deterministic repository-text coverage of specific forbidden\n   constructs rather than lint opinions or parse behavior.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` derives `GUARDED_WORKFLOWS` from the\n      `gerrit-verify.yaml` / `test.yml` local `uses:` transitive closure.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` asserts the existing guarded workflow list is\n      a floor of the derived set, so a seeded omission or newly wired reusable workflow fails the\n      coverage test.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` derives the CI-reachable make recipe set from workflow\n      `make` commands plus transitive `$(MAKE) <target>` recipe edges; on current main the set covers\n      `lint`, `typecheck`, `config-check`, `e2e-deps`, and `actionlint-bin` while excluding dev-only\n      targets not invoked by CI.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` statically scans those CI-reachable make recipes for\n      bash-only constructs (`set -o pipefail`, `[[ ... ]]`, arrays, `<<<`, `${var^}`, `${var,}`);\n      seeding `set -o pipefail` into a reachable recipe fails naming the offending construct and\n      recipe.\n- [ ] No scanner workflow or scanner install script is recreated, and no new required CI voting lane\n      is added. This ticket stays limited to unit-test coverage for the two surviving invariants.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED/held-out oracle: strengthen the two unit-test modules first, then confirm they fail for the\n  correct reason against current implementation (hardcoded guarded workflow set; missing static scan\n  for a seeded bash-only construct).\n- GREEN: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q`\n- Mutation teeth: temporarily reintroduce the escaped defects (hardcoded/omitted guarded workflow\n  coverage and `set -o pipefail` in a reachable recipe) and confirm the oracle goes RED, then restore.\n- Local gates: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and\n  `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788572190153535001,"uuid":"8b59a0fb-e0ed-45c8-848d-1cb38189cd4c"}